  "job_B14.24_20251003_114306": {
    "text": "Be witena ger\u00e6dnessan.\n\u00deis syndan \u00fea ger\u00e6dnessa, \u00fee Engla r\u00e6dgifan gecuran & gecw\u00e6dan & geornlice l\u00e6rdan, \u00fe\u00e6t man\n& \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00feonne \u00e6rest \u00fe\u00e6ra biscpa frumr\u00e6d, \u00fe\u00e6t we ealle fram synnum georne gecyrran, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee we don\n& witena ger\u00e6dnes is, \u00fe\u00e6t abbodas & abbodissan heora agen lif rihtlice fadian & eac heora heorda\n& \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6lces hades men georne gebugan for Gode & for worolde, \u00e6lc to \u00feam rihte \u00fee him to gebyrige.\n& huru\u00feinga Godes \u00feeowas biscpas & abbodas, munecas & mynecena, canonicas & nunnan to rihte\n& witena ger\u00e6dnes is, \u00fe\u00e6t muneca gehwilc, \u00fee ute of mynstre sy, & regoles ne gyme, do swa him \u00feearf\ngebuge georne into mynstre mid eallum ea\u00f0mettum & misd\u00e6da geswice & bete swy\u00fee georne \u00fe\u00e6t he\n& se munuc, \u00fee mynster n\u00e6bbe, cume to scirebiscop & trywsige hine sylfne wi\u00f0 God & wi\u00f0 men, \u00fe\u00e6t\n& gif he \u00fe\u00e6t gel\u00e6ste, \u00feonne bi\u00f0 he weor\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t hine man \u00fee bet healde, wunige \u00fe\u00e6r he wunige.\n& canonicas, \u00fe\u00e6r seo ar sy, \u00fe\u00e6t hy beodern & sl\u00e6pern habban magan, healdan heora mynster mid\n& ealle Godes \u00feeowas, & huru\u00feinga sacerdas, we bidda\u00f0 & l\u00e6ra\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t hy Gode hyran & cl\u00e6nnesse\nFulgeorne hi witan, \u00fe\u00e6t hy nagon mid rihte \u00feurh \u00e6nig h\u00e6med\u00feing wifes gemanan.\nAc hit is \u00fee wyrse, \u00fee sume habba\u00f0 twa o\u00f0\u00f0e ma, & sum, \u00feeh he forl\u00e6te \u00fea he \u00e6r h\u00e6fde, he be\n& se \u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6s geswican wille & cl\u00e6nnesse healdan, h\u00e6bbe he Godes miltse, & \u00fe\u00e6r to eacan to\n& se \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t nelle, \u00fe\u00e6t his hade gebyrige, wanige his weor\u00f0scipe \u00e6g\u00f0er ge for Gode ge for worolde.\n& la gyt we willa\u00f0 biddan freonda gehwylcne & eal folc eac l\u00e6ran georne, \u00fe\u00e6t hy inwerdre heortan\n& gif wiccan o\u00f0\u00f0e wigeleras, scincr\u00e6ftcan o\u00f0\u00f0e horcwenan, mor\u00f0wyrhtan o\u00f0\u00f0e mansworan ahwar\n& witena ger\u00e6dnes is, \u00fe\u00e6t man rihte laga up ar\u00e6re for Gode & for worolde & \u00e6ghwilce unlaga georne\n& witena ger\u00e6dnes is, \u00fe\u00e6t man Christene men & unforworhte of earde ne sylle, ne huru on h\u00e6\u00feene\n& witena ger\u00e6dnes is, \u00fe\u00e6t man Christene men for ealles to lytlan to dea\u00f0e ne forr\u00e6de.\nAc elles ger\u00e6de man fri\u00f0lice steora, folce to \u00feearfe, & ne forspille for lytlum Godes agen\nAc \u00e6ghwilce d\u00e6de toscade man w\u00e6rlice & dom \u00e6fter d\u00e6de medemige be m\u00e6\u00fee, swa for Gode sy\n& ge\u00feence swy\u00fee georne se \u00fee o\u00ferum deme, hw\u00e6s he sylf gyrne, \u00feonne he \u00feus cwe\u00f0e: Et dimitte\n& we l\u00e6ra\u00f0 swy\u00fee geornlice, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6ghwilc Christen man unriht h\u00e6med georne forbuge & Christene\n& \u00e6fre ne geweor\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t Christen man gewifige in VI manna sibf\u00e6ce on his agenum cynne, \u00fe\u00e6t is\nNe on gehalgodre \u00e6nigre nunnan, ne on his gef\u00e6deran, ne on \u00e6l\u00e6tan \u00e6nig Cristen man ne gewifige\nNe na ma wifa \u00feonne an h\u00e6bbe; ac beo be \u00fe\u00e6re anre, \u00fea hwile \u00fee heo libbe, se \u00fee wille Godes lage\n& sy \u00e6lc cyrice on Godes gri\u00fee & on \u00fe\u00e6s cynges & on ealles Cristenes folces.\n& sy \u00e6lc cyricgri\u00f0 binnan wagum & cyninges handgri\u00f0 efen unwemme.\n& \u00e6nig man heonan for\u00f0 cyrican ne \u00feowige, ne cyricmangunge mid unrihte ne macige, ne cyric\u00feen ne\n& gel\u00e6ste man Godes gerihta \u00e6ghwilce geare rihtlice georne, \u00fe\u00e6t is sulh\u00e6lmessan huru XV niht ofer\n& gif man \u00e6nig lic of rihtscire elles hwar lecge, gel\u00e6ste man \u00feone saulsceat swa \u00feeh into \u00feam mynstre,\n& ealle Godes gerihta fyr\u00ferige man georne, ealswa hit \u00feearf is.\n& freolsa & f\u00e6stena healde man rihtlice.\nSunnand\u00e6ges freols healde man georne, swa \u00fe\u00e6rto gebyrige; & cypinga & folcgemota & hunta\u00f0fara\n& sancta Marian heahfreolstida ealle weor\u00f0ige man georne, \u00e6rest mid f\u00e6stene & sy\u00fe\u00fean mid freolse.\n& to \u00e6ghwilces apostoles heahtide f\u00e6ste man georne, butan to Philippus & Iacobus freolse ne beode\nElles o\u00fere freolsa & f\u00e6stena healde man georne, swa swa \u00fea heoldan \u00fea \u00fee betst heoldan, & ymbren\n& f\u00e6ste man \u00e6lce Friged\u00e6ge, butan hit freols sy.\n& ordal & a\u00feas & wifunga \u00e6fre syndan tocwedene heahfreolsdagum & rihtymbrenum & fram\n& beo \u00feam halgan tidan, ealswa hit riht is, eallum Cristenum mannum sibb & som gem\u00e6ne, & \u00e6lc\n& gif hwa o\u00f0rum scyle borh o\u00f0\u00f0e bote \u00e6t woroldlican \u00feingan, gel\u00e6ste hit him georne \u00e6r o\u00f0\u00f0on \u00e6fter.\n& sy \u00e6lc wydewe, \u00fee hy sylfe mid rihte gehealde, on Godes gri\u00f0e & on \u00fe\u00e6s cynges.\n& sitte \u00e6lc XII mona\u00f0 werleas; ceose sy\u00fe\u00fean \u00fe\u00e6t heo sylf wille.\n& \u00e6ghwilc Christen man do, swa him \u00feearf is: gyme his Christendomes georne & gewunige gelomlice\n& gearwige eac to huslgange huru \u00feriwa on geare gehwa hine sylfne, \u00fee his agene \u00feearfe wille\n& word & weorc freonda gehwilc fadige mid rihte & a\u00f0 & wedd w\u00e6rlice healde.\n& \u00e6ghwilc unriht aweorpe man georne of \u00feysan earde, \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee man don m\u00e6ge.\n& swicollice d\u00e6da & la\u00f0lice unlaga ascunige man swy\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t is false gewihta & woge gemeta &\n& la understande man georne, \u00fe\u00e6t eal swylc is to leanne & n\u00e6fre to lufianne.\nAc lufige man Godes riht heonan for\u00fe georne wordes & weorces; \u00feonne wyr\u00f0 \u00feysse \u00feeode sona God\nWutan eac ealle ymbe fri\u00fees bote & ymbe feos bote smeagean swy\u00f0e georne: swa ymbe fri\u00fees bote,\n& gemeta & gewihta rihte man georne, & \u00e6lces unrihtes heonan for\u00f0 geswice.\n& burhbota & bricbota aginne man georne on \u00e6ghwilcon ende, & fyrdunga eac & scipfyrdunga\n& w\u00e6rlic bi\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t man \u00e6ghwilce geare sona \u00e6fter eastron fyrdscipa gearwige.\n& gyf hwa folces fyrdscip awyrde, gebete \u00fe\u00e6t georne, & cyninge \u00fea munde; & gif hit man amyrre, \u00fe\u00e6t\n& gif hwa of fyrde butan leafe gewende, \u00fee cyning sylf on sy, plihte his are.\n& gif mor\u00f0wyrhtan o\u00f0\u00f0e mansworan o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00e6b\u00e6re manslagan to \u00feam ge\u00feristian, \u00fe\u00e6t hy on \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges\n& gyf hwa ymbe cyninges feorh syrwe, sy he his feores scyldig & ealles \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee he age, gif hit him\n& gif hwa forsteal ongean lahriht Cristes o\u00fe\u00fee cyninges ahwar gewyrce, gylde wer o\u00fe\u00fee wite be \u00feam \u00fee\n& gif hwa nunnan gewemme o\u00fe\u00fee wydewan nydn\u00e6me, gebete \u00fe\u00e6t deope for Gode & for worolde.\n& smeage man symle on \u00e6ghwilce wisan, hu man fyrmest m\u00e6ge r\u00e6d aredian, \u00feeode to \u00feearfe, & rihtne\nFor\u00feam \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t hit sceal on earde godian to ahte, \u00fee man unriht alecge & rihtwisnesse lufige for\nNu wille we eac l\u00e6ran Godes \u00feeowas georne, \u00fe\u00e6t hy huru hy sylfe w\u00e6rlice be\u00feencan & \u00feurh Godes\nEac we gyt willa\u00f0 myngian georne freonda gehwilcne, ealswa us neod is gelome to donne, \u00fe\u00e6t gehwa\n& \u00fe\u00e6t he oft & gelome h\u00e6bbe on gemynde, \u00fe\u00e6t mannum is m\u00e6st \u00feearf oftost to gemunene, \u00fe\u00e6t is\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy rihtne Christendom rihtlice healdan & \u00fe\u00e6t hy godcundan lareawan geornlice hyran &\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy Godes cyrican \u00e6ghwar georne gri\u00f0ian & fri\u00feian & mid leohte & lacum hi gelome gegretan,\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy Godes gerihta \u00e6ghwylce geare mid rihte gel\u00e6stan & freolsa & f\u00e6stena rihtlice healdan.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy Sunnandaga cypinga & folciscra gemota georne geswican.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy Godes \u00feeowas symle werian & weor\u00f0ian.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy Godes \u00feearfan frefrian & fedan.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy wydewan & steopcild to oft ne ahw\u00e6nan, ac georne hy gladian.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy \u00e6l\u00feeodige men & feorran cumene ne tyrian ne ne tynan.\n& \u00fe\u00e6t hy o\u00ferum mannum unriht ne beodan ealles to swy\u00fee; ac manna gehwylc o\u00ferum beode \u00fe\u00e6t riht,\n& se \u00fee ahwar heonan for\u00f0 rihte laga wyrde, Godes o\u00fe\u00feon manna, gebete hit georne, swa hw\u00e6\u00feer swa\n& gif for godbotan feohbot arise\u00f0, swa swa wise woroldwitan to steore gesettan, \u00fe\u00e6t gebyre\u00f0 rihtlice,\n& a swa man bi\u00f0 mihtigra her am for worulde o\u00fe\u00feon \u00feurh ge\u00feing\u00f0a hearra on hade, swa sceal he\n& \u00fey man sceal medmian & gescadlice toscadan, ge on godcunda scriftan ge on woroldcundan steoran,\n& gif hit geweor\u00fee\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t man unwilles o\u00fe\u00fee ungewealdes \u00e6nig \u00feing misde\u00f0, na bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t na gelic \u00feam\n\u00c6lce d\u00e6de toscade man w\u00e6rlice & a dom be d\u00e6de fadige mid rihte & medemige be m\u00e6\u00fee for Gode &",
